<title>MEXICO: Mexico decentralizes highway maintenance.</title>
<headline>Mexico decentralizes highway maintenance.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Communications and Transportation Ministry said Monday it has signed a series of 28 agreements with state governments that will decentralize the construction and repair of rural highways.</p>
<p>States will assume responsibility for rural roads as of 1997 as part of a pledge by President Ernesto Zedillo to return authority to the states, the ministry said in a news release.  State government also are expected to be more attuned to the greatest local needs, the news release said.</p>
<p>The ministry also said that it has generated 19 million work days this year for 140,000 workers in rural zones where 350 million pesos were invested.</p>
<p>--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom, (525) 728-9507</p>
